Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||10-21-2001||12:45 AM||||Ever since i have had my car (couple of months) the power windows, both of them go really really SLOW!<BR>the dew strips are very stiff, and the windows have scratch marks from possbily stripped brushings. How do i fix my problem? Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||10-21-2001||03:13 AM||||remove the inner door panel to access the window rails. Clean and lubricate them thoroughly and that should help. Also, you might change the dew strips while you have the inner door panel off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-21-2001||07:30 PM||||Yea, I agree. THe only thing that makes them run slow is : a/ lube is dried up b/motor is bad.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hippocrat||10-22-2001||05:43 AM||||Just on the off chance (not to disagree with what's been said)<BR>especially with the scratch marks you mentioned.<P>I noticed this problem with mine a while ago.<BR>With mine it turned out to be a bad body ground. Didn't really think of it as a ground problem at first because everything else seemed to be fine. Fixed the ground wire and they have been flying up and down every since.<P>Chalked it up to the amperage the windows draw. <BR>Just a thought.<p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||10-22-2001||06:40 AM||||Mine are slow, too.. where is this ground wire you checked? Near the door hinges, or elsewhere in the harness?<P>Thanks...<P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000005||Matthew_Fiero||10-22-2001||08:30 AM||||Yes, where is this ground wire?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||10-22-2001||08:59 AM||||Yup, cuz after I check that ground wire, I'm gonna have to pull the door panels and lube my tracks, if they're still slow....||||reg||5
Z||000007||Joe Torma||10-22-2001||11:12 AM||||I think my motors are just slow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>Isn't there a spring in there somewhere?  Maybe its weak? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||10-22-2001||11:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Matthew_Fiero:<BR><B>Yes, where is this ground wire?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That ground I think is behind the passenger side kick panel at foot level. 1, 2 or 3 wires may be attached to it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||10-22-2001||07:30 PM||||I seem to have the same problum. I found out what it was though. I wasn't spining the window crank fast enough... Oh wait, Never Mind  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000010||voyagerspe||10-22-2001||08:06 PM||||IT COULD BE BAD SWITCHES <BR>sorry didnt mean to yell   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Dont take your door apart this is how you test them.<P>1. disconnect the door harness from the body harness (right by the under dash courtisy light)<P>2. get 2 pieces  of wire and connect them to a 12volt power source.<P>3. Touch each wire to the outside (heavy) wire on the door harness connector<BR>  Reverse the wires to go up and down.<P>4. If the windows are still slow the problems in the door and you have to rip it open   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>but if there quick its a bad switch or wire or connection.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by voyagerspe (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||Hippocrat||10-22-2001||10:45 PM||||Sorry should have mentioned which one it was.<P>On mine it was the ground running from the battery to the frame. It wasn't making a decent connection.<P>I also agree with voyagerspe. I would definitely check the switches before pulling the panel off the door. That IMHO would be the last resort. Could avoid a lot of frustration <P>But hey at least with the Fieros the door skin bolts off. Sure makes swapping out the motor a WHOLE lot easier than on other cars.||||reg||1
